077.JPG 1 I hike a long distance from the train station to Burg Rheinstein
078.JPG 2 Rheinstein is a castle still intact, furnished, and is in contrast to most of the ruins on the Rhine
079.JPG 1 The vinyards there make use of a small trolly to navigate the hill, how fun!
080.JPG 1 Full suits of armor, and much bric-a-brac in the castle
081.JPG 1 Wooden spiral staircase, a photo must-have
082.JPG 1 The view from this castle is spectacular. The last owner, before private purchase, was a Duchess of Mecklenburg
083.JPG 1 Rheinstein's walled garden is lush, the vineyards are just beyond.
085.JPG 1 I quickly travel to Mainz, a modern city in germany. I trek in full gear. I move with focused intensity, never missing a good snapshot. Where is waldo in this picture?
087.JPG 1 The red sandstone cathedral in Mainz is a fresh contrast to most European architecture.
090.JPG 1 I arrive at the Eurographics conference. We play foosball -- at full scale.
093.JPG 1 The conference reception is in the Völklingen Ironworks, Saarbruecken. Here is a great flywheel.
094.JPG 1 The machinery is from another age. This Demag, It inspires. 
095.JPG 1 Another view of the machinery in the Völklingen Ironworks.
096.JPG 1 Outside, rust covered pipes, the Völklingen Ironworks.
